# Repository Architecture: `sharedmodule` is Primary

The core runtime codebase for **Mitz Mode** (Android + iOS) is housed in **`sharedmodule/`**.

## Workspace Structure & Repositories

1. **`sharedmodule/` — PRIMARY REPO (One Source of Truth)**
   - Git remote: `https://github.com/Geulanow613/sharedmodule.git` (branch `main`).
   - Contains all Kotlin Multiplatform (KMP) shared code: Compose UI screens, Siddur liturgy & reader engine, zmanim, calendar calculations, domain models, tests, and Compose Resources.
   - **Runtime bundled translations**: `sharedmodule/shared/src/commonMain/composeResources/files/translations/he.json` (and other languages) is the actual file loaded by the apps at runtime.
   - Both Android (`MitzModeAndroid`) and iOS (`mitzmodeios`) consume `sharedmodule/shared` directly.

2. **`c:\apps\hehehe\` (Root Workspace) — `Mitzmodeandroid` Repo**
   - Git remote: `https://github.com/Geulanow613/Mitzmodeandroid.git` (branch `master`).
   - Host workspace containing the Android app shell (`:app`), Gradle root configuration, baseline profile, and gitignores the nested `sharedmodule/` repo checkout.

3. **`be-a-tzaddik/` — SECONDARY / TOOLING & DATA CATALOG**
   - Auxiliary tooling and source catalog repository.
   - Houses human translation catalog shards (`be-a-tzaddik/data/translation-catalog/human/`) and data generation/merge scripts (`be-a-tzaddik/tools/`).
   - When updating translations, shards are edited in `be-a-tzaddik/` and compiled/merged directly into `sharedmodule/shared/src/commonMain/composeResources/files/translations/he.json`.

## Hard Rules for Agents

- **Always prioritize `sharedmodule` for app logic & resources**: Any feature, bug fix, liturgy adjustment, UI text, or translation change that runs in the app must be present in `sharedmodule/`.
- **Separate Git Repositories**:
  - `sharedmodule` has its own `.git` directory (`origin/main`). Committing in the root `Mitzmodeandroid` workspace does **NOT** commit changes in `sharedmodule`.
  - Always run git commands (`git status`, `git diff`, `git commit`, `git push`) inside `sharedmodule/` when modifying shared code or runtime translations.
- **Do not duplicate or fork**: Never copy code between `be-a-tzaddik/shared` and `sharedmodule/shared` manually; treat `sharedmodule` as the definitive authority.
